  "panels": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "How to read this dashboard",
      "id": 1,
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 11
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "### Alerts overview: every Prometheus alert of the lab in one place\n**Why this dashboard exists.** Alertmanager is deployed but routes everything to the `null` receiver on purpose (no\nSlack/e-mail noise while the lab is built). Alerts still **evaluate** in Prometheus: this dashboard and the\n*Active alerts for this service* table at the top of every service dashboard are where they are seen.\n\n**States.** *Pending*: the rule's condition is true but has not lasted the rule's `for` yet (may clear by itself).\n*Firing*: the condition held for the whole `for` window: something needs a look. Severity follows the upstream rule\n(`critical` = user-visible or about to be, `warning` = degraded or a risk).\n\n**How to use it.** 1) The stats say whether anything is wrong now. 2) The table lists each active alert with its labels\n(namespace, pod, job…) and how long it has been active. 3) *Firing alerts over time* and *Most frequent alerts* show\nflapping or chronic alerts that deserve a fix (or a better threshold). 4) Open the service dashboard (folders by tool\ngroup) and read the alert's rule: `kubectl --context k8s01 get prometheusrule -A` or the rule files in the repo;\nkube-prometheus-stack alerts link their runbook at https://runbooks.prometheus-operator.dev/.\n\n**Always on, by design:** `Watchdog` (proves the pipeline works; hidden here) and `InfoInhibitor`.\nData: Prometheus `ALERTS` / `ALERTS_FOR_STATE` series ([docs](https://prometheus.io/docs/prometheus/latest/configuration/alerting_rules/#inspecting-alerts-during-runtime))."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Critical firing",
      "id": 2,
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "description": "Alerts with severity=critical in state firing. Anything above 0 needs action now.",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 11,
        "w": 6,
        "h": 4
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "count(ALERTS{alertname!~\"Watchdog|InfoInhibitor\", severity=~\"$severity\", namespace=~\"$namespace\", alertstate=\"firing\", severity=\"critical\"}) or vector(0)",
          "legendFormat": "",
          "instant": true,
          "range": false
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "unit": "none",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "textMode": "value",
        "justifyMode": "center",
        "orientation": "auto",
        "wideLayout": true
